{"kind":"stack","id":"levers-pulleys-gears","title":"Levers, pulleys and gears: smaller force, bigger effect","theme":{"background":"#f4f7fb","foreground":"#1d2b3a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-term","content":"Lever"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-def","content":"A bar that turns around a fixed point called the pivot. A small push on one end can lift a heavy load on the other end."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"A lever helps us because it lets us use a smaller force to do what?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Lift a heavy load more easily","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Make the load weigh less","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Stop the load from moving","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Where is the pivot of a seesaw?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"In the middle, where it rests on the support","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"At the very end of one seat","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Under the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-term","content":"Pulley"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-def","content":"A wheel with a rope running over it. Pulling the rope down can lift a load up, and a pulley can make lifting easier."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"A pulley system with several wheels lets you lift a load by pulling with what?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"A smaller force, but you pull the rope a longer distance","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"A bigger force, over a shorter distance","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"The same force, with no change in distance","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"castle"},{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"A knight must raise the castle drawbridge, but it is very heavy. He can use a pulley or a lever. Which will he choose?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Use the pulley","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Use the lever","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The knight loops the rope over the pulley wheels. He pulls, and the drawbridge rises slowly but steadily."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The knight places a long beam under the drawbridge and pushes down on its far end. The drawbridge lifts up around the pivot."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Gears are wheels with teeth. When a small gear turns a large gear, what happens to the turning force?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"It becomes greater, but the large gear turns more slowly","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"It becomes smaller, and the large gear turns faster","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"It stays exactly the same","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"You finished the lesson on levers, pulleys and gears!"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"Well done. Remember: these machines let a smaller force have a greater effect."}],"actions":[]}}
